   "text": "**About the 48-hour window:** that's Forkful's set deadline for reporting missing or wrong items, and I have to apply it the same way to every order. It lets us check a problem while the delivery and restaurant records are still fresh. I understand it's frustrating when you don't notice something until later, and I'm sorry I can't make an exception for the churros.\n\n**Pho Real (K-6104):** You have already been refunded for the iced coffee. Our records show the restaurant marked it unavailable at 12:20 PM, before the courier picked up your order. Forkful then automatically refunded **$4.75** to your Visa ending 4242 at 12:21 PM. Since that refund already covers the iced coffee, I can't compensate it again. If you don't see the refund yet, it should show on your statement within a few business days.\n\n**Summary of everything today:**\n- **Saffron Lane (K-6101):** $12.00 credit (late delivery) + $5.40 credit (missing lassi)\n- **Burger Barn (K-6102):** $11.00 refund to your Visa (wrong burger)\n- **Taqueria Luz (K-6103):** reported after the 48-hour window, so no compensation\n- **Pho Real (K-6104):** iced coffee already refunded automatically ($4.75)\n- **Account credit balance:** $17.40\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so the iced coffee was already refunded automatically? I never saw that refund, and I was never told the restaurant had marked it unavailable. Could you check whether the $4.75 refund is actually on the Visa ending 4242? I'd like to be sure it went through.\n\nOtherwise, thanks for going through everything. I'll wait for the refund and the credit to show up."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked our payment record for the Pho Real order (K-6104), and the refund is there:\n\n- **$4.75 refund for the iced coffee**, sent to your **Visa ending 4242**\n- Issued automatically at **12:21 PM today**, because the restaurant marked the item unavailable\n\nSo the refund went through on our side. Card refunds can take a few business days to appear on your statement, which is probably why you don't see it yet. I'm sorry nobody told you the iced coffee was unavailable. That would have been confusing when it didn't show up.\n\n**One more thing you might notice:** each order also has a temporary authorization hold from when it was placed. All of those holds have been released, so you won't be charged for them. They'll drop off your statement within a few business days, and only the final charges stand.\n\n**What to expect:**\n- **$17.40 account credit:** already on your account and ready for your next order\n- **$11.00 refund (Burger Barn):** 3\u20135 business days to your Visa\n- **$4.75 refund (Pho Real):** already issued; should appear within a few business days\n\nThanks for your patience going through all of this, Hannah. I hope next week goes better with Forkful."
